 "termination": "answer",
 "final_answer": "In the precomputed SCAPS-1D absorber-thickness sweep (NIP stack: Spiro-like HTL / perovskite / TiO2-like ETL; perovskite Eg 1.55 eV, \u00b5n=\u00b5p=1 cm\u00b2/Vs, Nt 1e14 cm\u207b\u00b3; only absorber thickness varied, 200\u20131000 nm, 8 points):\n\n- **200 nm:** PCE = **24.29 %** (Voc = 1.4001 V, Jsc = 19.14 mA/cm\u00b2, FF = 90.62 %)\n- **1000 nm:** PCE = **32.14 %** (Voc = 1.3645 V, Jsc = 26.06 mA/cm\u00b2, FF = 90.40 %)\n\n**How PCE changes with thickness:** monotonic increase, no interior peak; the maximum is at the largest swept point (1000 nm), so the sweep only brackets the peak from below and never turns over. Total change 200\u21921000 nm is **+7.85 percentage points (+32.3 % relative)**.\n\nFull sweep (d nm | Voc | Jsc | FF | PCE):\n200 | 1.4001 | 19.14 | 90.62 | 24.29\n300 | 1.3924 | 22.09 | 90.62 | 27.88\n400 | 1.3865 | 23.69 | 90.58 | 29.75 (reference cell)\n500 | 1.3817 | 24.61 | 90.53 | 30.79\n600 | 1.3773 | 25.17 | 90.50 | 31.38\n700 | 1.3734 | 25.54 | 90.49 | 31.73\n800 | 1.3700 | 25.78 | 90.46 | 31.95\n1000 | 1.3645 | 26.06 | 90.40 | 32.14\n\nMechanism and shape: Jsc rises strongly (19.14 \u2192 26.06 mA/cm\u00b2, +36 %) and dominates, while Voc drops slightly (\u20130.036 V, \u20132.5 %) and FF is essentially flat (\u20130.23 points). Returns diminish sharply \u2014 step gains of +3.59, +1.87, +1.03, +0.60, +0.35, +0.21, then only +0.20 pp over the last 200 nm (~0.10 pp/100 nm), so thick absorbers are clearly sub-optimal and 1000 nm is near the saturation point.\n\nCaveats: this is simulation only (no measured device); the sweep file records no solver-convergence state; no points exist beyond 1000 nm, so the true maximum location is unresolved (any peak past 1000 nm would be small \u2014 an extrapolation, not simulated data); live SCAPS was disabled in this environment, so no re-runs or denser grids were possible.",
